## 3. Log review routine (for your README)

A repeatable review you can run daily or after an incident. These are the commands, not just the theory:

| Question | Command |
|---|---|
| Warnings or worse this boot? | `sudo journalctl -p warning -b --no-pager \| tail -30` |
| Who logged in, and with which key? | `sudo journalctl -u ssh --since today --no-pager \| grep -E 'Accepted\|Failed\|Invalid'` |
| Who used sudo? | `sudo journalctl _COMM=sudo --since today --no-pager` |
| What did the firewall block? | `sudo journalctl -k --since today --no-pager \| grep 'UFW BLOCK' \| tail` |
| Who is banned right now? | `sudo fail2ban-client status sshd` |
| Failed authentication summary | `sudo aureport --failed --summary` |
| Identity file changes | `sudo ausearch -k identity -ts today -i` |
| Config tampering | `sudo ausearch -k sshd -k sudoers -k firewall -ts today -i` |
| Recent logins | `last -n 10` and `sudo lastb \| head` |

