## 4. Validation checklist

| # | Host | Command | Expected |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | Bastion | `chronyc tracking \| head -5` | A real reference, `Leap status : Normal` |
| 2 | Bastion | `sudo ss -ulpn \| grep ':123'` | chronyd listening |
| 3 | Bastion | `sudo ufw status numbered \| grep 123` | Allowed only from `10.10.10.20` |
| 4 | Target | `timedatectl timesync-status` (NAT **disconnected**) | `Server: 10.10.10.10`, small offset |
| 5 | Target | `timedatectl \| grep synchronized` | `System clock synchronized: yes` |
| 6 | Both | `date -u` on each, compared | Within about a second |
| 7 | Target | `sudo ufw status numbered \| grep 123` | Only `to 10.10.10.10 ... 123/udp` |
| 8 | Both | `journalctl --disk-usage` and `ls -ld /var/log/journal` | Directory exists, usage under 500M |
| 9 | Both | `journalctl --list-boots \| wc -l` (after reboot) | 2 or more (history survived the reboot) |
| 10 | Both | `grep -E '^(max_log_file\|num_logs\|max_log_file_action) ' /etc/audit/auditd.conf` | `50`, `5`, `ROTATE` |
| 11 | Both | `cat /proc/cmdline \| grep -o 'audit=1'` | `audit=1` |
| 12 | Target | `sudo auditctl -l \| wc -l` | Roughly 40 rules, no load errors |
| 13 | Both | `sudo auditctl -s \| grep -E 'enabled\|lost'` | `enabled 2`, `lost 0` |
| 14 | Both | `sudo auditctl -e 1` | Refused (immutable) |
| 15 | Target | Step H file test | Events visible with `auid=secadmin` |
| 16 | Target | Failed-login `ausearch` / `aureport` | The `baduser` attempt appears |
| 17 | Bastion | `sudo ausearch -k bastion-keys -i -ts today \| tail` | Shows key-related file activity (may be empty until you touch `~/.ssh`) |
| 18 | Target | `sudo ls -ld /var/log/audit; sudo ls -l /var/log/audit/audit.log` | Directory `750`, log `600`, both root |
| 19 | Target | `ip route` | No default route (NAT closed) |
| 20 | Both | `ssh target hostname` from the Bastion, plus `sudo ufw status` and `systemctl is-active fail2ban` on the Target | Still all working |


